fuzzy.library/FuzzyAddEntry                        fuzzy.library/FuzzyAddEntry

   NAME
        FuzzyAddEntry -- Add a file or drawer to an index being written
            (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        ok = FuzzyAddEntry(writer, entry)
        D0                A0      A1

        LONG FuzzyAddEntry(FuzzyWriter *, struct FuzzyEntry *);

   FUNCTION
        Writes one entry: Path (PathLen bytes, or -1 for up to its 0),
        Type, Prot, Size and Date. NameOffset is not used (readers work it
        out). Add a drawer's entries, then walk into its drawers:
        neighbours sharing their path keep the index small.

   INPUTS
        writer - from FuzzyNewIndex()
        entry  - the entry

   RESULT
        ok - TRUE, or FALSE (the path is over 1024 bytes, or writing failed)

   SEE ALSO
        FuzzyNewIndex](#fuzzynewindex), FuzzyEndIndex


fuzzy.library/FuzzyAddVolume                      fuzzy.library/FuzzyAddVolume

   NAME
        FuzzyAddVolume -- Name a volume an index covers (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        error = FuzzyAddVolume(writer, name, date)
        D0                     A0      A1    D0

        LONG FuzzyAddVolume(FuzzyWriter *, CONST_STRPTR, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
        Records a volume (its name without the colon, and its date) in the
        index's header, so a reader can tell which disks it covers. All
        volumes must come before the first entry.

   INPUTS
        writer - from FuzzyNewIndex()
        name   - "Work" (up to 255 bytes)
        date   - the volume's date, seconds since 1978-01-01 (0 if unknown)

   RESULT
        error - FERR_OK, or FERR_ORDER (an entry came already),
                FERR_NOMEM (over 64 volumes)

   SEE ALSO
        FuzzyVolume](#fuzzyvolume)


fuzzy.library/FuzzyCloseIndex                    fuzzy.library/FuzzyCloseIndex

   NAME
        FuzzyCloseIndex -- Close an index (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        FuzzyCloseIndex(index)
                        A0

        VOID FuzzyCloseIndex(struct FuzzyIndex *);

   FUNCTION
        Closes the file and frees the handle. Hits from FuzzySearch() stay
        valid (they are copies).

   INPUTS
        index - from FuzzyOpenIndex(); NULL is safe

   SEE ALSO
        FuzzyOpenIndex](#fuzzyopenindex)


fuzzy.library/FuzzyEndIndex                        fuzzy.library/FuzzyEndIndex

   NAME
        FuzzyEndIndex -- Finish (or throw away) an index being written
            (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        error = FuzzyEndIndex(writer, keep)
        D0                    A0      D0

        LONG FuzzyEndIndex(FuzzyWriter *, LONG);

   FUNCTION
        keep TRUE: writes the entry count into the header, closes
        NAME.new, deletes the old NAME and renames NAME.new to NAME. keep
        FALSE: closes and deletes NAME.new, the old index stays. The
        writer is freed either way.

   INPUTS
        writer - from FuzzyNewIndex()
        keep   - TRUE to keep it

   RESULT
        error - FERR_OK, or FERR_IO (writing or renaming failed: NAME.new is
                deleted, the old index stays)

        Notes: Always call it, also to give up: it frees the writer.

   SEE ALSO
        FuzzyNewIndex](#fuzzynewindex)


fuzzy.library/FuzzyErrorText                      fuzzy.library/FuzzyErrorText

   NAME
        FuzzyErrorText -- An error in words (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        text = FuzzyErrorText(error)
        D0                    D0

        CONST_STRPTR FuzzyErrorText(LONG);

   FUNCTION
        Returns an English text for an FERR_ code: "the index is not
        there", "not a FuzzyFind index"...

   INPUTS
        error - FERR_OK ... FERR_ORDER

   RESULT
        text - read-only; "unknown error" for other numbers


